WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.471
You cannot reliably detect, investigate, or explain activity that you cannot observe.

00:00:06.471 --> 00:00:17.734
OT blind spots carry operational consequences because an unseen system may control equipment, provide operator visibility, or bridge a critical communication path.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:22.767
Missing evidence delays decisions when time and safety matter.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:29.238
Telemetry supports asset inventory by revealing devices, roles, protocols, peers, and dependencies.

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:39.543
Observation can identify undocumented or dormant assets returning to service, but it does not replace engineering records or physical verification.

00:00:39.543 --> 00:00:45.055
Devices that do not communicate during collection may remain invisible.

00:00:45.055 --> 00:00:53.922
During incident response, telemetry helps reconstruct timelines, accounts, sessions, affected assets, commands, configuration changes, and process conditions.

00:00:53.922 --> 00:01:04.707
Vulnerability teams can use observed reachability and asset criticality to prioritize findings rather than treating every vulnerable product as equally exposed.

00:01:04.707 --> 00:01:07.343
Business continuity also benefits.

00:01:07.343 --> 00:01:19.086
Communication loss, failed collection, degraded redundancy, unusual process trends, or inaccessible remote sites may indicate a cyber event, equipment failure, or network problem.

00:01:19.086 --> 00:01:23.640
Shared evidence lets teams coordinate diagnosis and recovery.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.672
IT and OT telemetry overlap, but their emphasis differs.

00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:35.143
IT sources commonly focus on users, endpoints, cloud services, and business applications.

00:01:35.143 --> 00:01:44.969
OT telemetry adds controllers, industrial protocols, field communications, process values, engineering activity, and long-lived devices with limited native logging.

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:48.564
More data is not automatically better.

00:01:48.564 --> 00:01:57.910
Useful telemetry is selected around operational questions, collected safely, retained appropriately, and enriched with asset and process context.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:07.257
The objective is enough trustworthy evidence to reduce uncertainty without burdening sensitive systems or analysts with unmanaged noise.
